{"text": "This Month al Herrtage\n\nTHE HERITAGE FOUNDATION\u00a2 214 MASSACHUSETTS AVENUE, N.E. WASHINGTON, D.C. 20002 \u00ab (202) 546-4400\nOCTOBER 1983 CONTACT: Joyce Hemenway\n\nIN WASHINGTON\n\nLectures/Debates:\n* Richard V. Allen, Heritage Distinguished Fellow and\nformer national security advisor to President Reagan,\nwill speak on the West's leadership role in the world at\nthe Annual Friends and Alumni Conference of the Inter-\ncollegiate Studies Institute. 11:00 a.m. at the\nSheraton-Washington Hotel. By invitation only. Con-\ntact: Averil Stoneback, 737-2824. October 1\n\n* Dr. Juliana Pilon, Heritage United Nations analyst, will\nlecture on how the PLO uses the U.N. in the first of a\nseries of lectures on the PLO, sponsored by the Commit-\ntee for Accuracy in Middle East Reporting in America.\nAt the Jewish Community Center, 6125 Montrose Road,\nRockville, Md. Open to the public. Contact: Elaine\nMann, 881-0100. October 2\n\n*\n\nExecutive Vice President Phil Truluck, Senior Fellow\nCol. Ted Crackel, and Director of Legislative Informa-\ntion Virginia Gilbert will discuss the policymaking\nprocess with a group of senior military officers--\nstudents and faculty members--from the U.S. Army War\nCollege. Colonel Crackel, director of Heritage\u2019s ongo-\ning \"military reform\" study project, is former director\nof military history and strategy studies at the college.\n9:00 to 11:30 a.m. at Heritage. Private. Contact:\nLynn Johnson, ext 559. October 4\n\n* Peter Germanis, Heritage Schultz Fellow, will testify\nbefore the Task Force on Entitlements and Human Assis-\ntance Programs regarding the scope and impact of federal\ndomestic entitlement programs. The task force is a\nproject of the House Republican Research Committee. 9\na.m. to 1 p.m. in 2337 Rayburn Senate Office Building.\nOpen to the public. Contact: Connie Heckman, 225-2132. October 4\n\n%\n\nHeritage Vice President for Research Burton Yale Pines\nwill present a conservative domestic policy agenda to\nthe National Jewish Student Conference on Public Policy\nIssues. 11:30 a.m. at the Shoreham Hotel. Closed\nmeeting. Contact: Michele Bernstein, 857-6560. October 7",
